(5852878, 850105, 56880, '<td valign="top">This is a great photograph; I like how the boy is lit by light from the window, as he and the giraffe ponder what could have been were it not for the window separating them.  However this private, secluded moment doesn''t capture the essence of a main road.  As others have noted, in a different challenge this would have scored higher.</td>', 'This is a great photograph; I like how the boy is lit by light from the window, as he and the giraffe ponder what could have been were it not for the window separating them.  However this private, secluded moment doesn''t capture the essence of a main road.  As others have noted, in a different challenge this would have scored higher.', '2010-02-04 13:46:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5852881, 849477, 56880, '<td valign="top">Ah, Berkeley.  I lived in a basement on Durant just a block south of Telegraph while I was attending Cal.  The tilt to the left might be lost on those unfamiliar with Berkeley politics.  There are a lot of distracting elements in the photograph, such as the heavy clouds and the lead car (being in better light than the bumper sticker seller).  It does capture how I remember that side of Berkeley.</td>', 'Ah, Berkeley.  I lived in a basement on Durant just a block south of Telegraph while I was attending Cal.  The tilt to the left might be lost on those unfamiliar with Berkeley politics.  There are a lot of distracting elements in the photograph, such as the heavy clouds and the lead car (being in better light than the bumper sticker seller).  It does capture how I remember that side of Berkeley.', '2010-02-04 13:51:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5852911, 850125, 56880, '<td valign="top">The road and left side of the house are very nicely lit, but the right half of the photograph appears very flat in comparison, and detracts from the better part of the image.  The red ribbons on the lightposts offer a splash of color, complimenting the rich brown of the left tree.</td>', 'The road and left side of the house are very nicely lit, but the right half of the photograph appears very flat in comparison, and detracts from the better part of the image.  The red ribbons on the lightposts offer a splash of color, complimenting the rich brown of the left tree.', '2010-02-04 14:33:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5852959, 850105, 66384, '<td valign="top">Wendy, I think you got excellent feed back during the challenge. Some people, who are sticklers for the litteral meaning of the challenge title, gave it DNMC. Some people thought it was wonderfully appropriate and very touching, but all seemed to agree it is a very good photo. Don''t fret the score, I think the low votes were due to DNMC, which just isn''t so.</td>', 'Wendy, I think you got excellent feed back during the challenge. Some people, who are sticklers for the litteral meaning of the challenge title, gave it DNMC. Some people thought it was wonderfully appropriate and very touching, but all seemed to agree it is a very good photo. Don''t fret the score, I think the low votes were due to DNMC, which just isn''t so.', '2010-02-04 15:21:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5853066, 850109, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB</b> <br/> <br/>Well, <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=113634" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">kellmak10</a> you may be new to photography but you have a good eye and an excellent grasp of photographic storytelling.  <br/> <br/>So, you don''t have much of a downtown.  So you took what you had and told a story about your town and processed it in excellently in black &amp; white.  You''ve talked about a busy highway, truck traffic, train crossings and a community church, all without being cluttered or messy.  <br/> <br/>Anyhow, I''m supposed to critique your image (that''s what this DPC club is for) so here goes:  IMO - Don''t change a thing.<br/> <br/>Eventually the high scores will come - or not.  Look up <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Posthumous</a>''s work for another very exciting angle at this photography obsession of ours.<br/> <br/>Okay, good work, sorry it didn''t score well.  Keep ''em coming.<br/> <br/>I hope this little critique was helpful to you.<br/>Alice</td>', 'GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB  Well,  kellmak10 you may be new to photography but you have a good eye and an excellent grasp of photographic storytelling.   So, you don''t have much of a downtown.  So you took what you had and told a story about your town and processed it in excellently in black & white.  You''ve talked about a busy highway, truck traffic, train crossings and a community church, all without being cluttered or messy.   Anyhow, I''m supposed to critique your image (that''s what this DPC club is for) so here goes:  IMO - Don''t change a thing. Eventually the high scores will come - or not.  Look up  Posthumous''s work for another very exciting angle at this photography obsession of ours. Okay, good work, sorry it didn''t score well.  Keep ''em coming. I hope this little critique was helpful to you.Alice', '2010-02-04 17:06:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5853156, 850056, 42345, '<td valign="top">The depth in this photo sucks you into it, and there is so much to see, yet it''s not messy,  Well done, congrats.</td>', 'The depth in this photo sucks you into it, and there is so much to see, yet it''s not messy,  Well done, congrats.', '2010-02-04 18:21:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5853259, 850056, 82707, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Fabulous image!  Congrats on the Blue!</td>', 'Wow!  Fabulous image!  Congrats on the Blue!', '2010-02-04 20:02:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5853301, 849481, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that this is a busy scene. The buildings hold interest and then we have the light trails too.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> this is good. Exposure of the lights is good. Given the light trails are what you were concentrating on the composition is ok - I find that the bright area at the left end of the light trails is where I start looking and then flow along to the right - this seems backwards to how you''d want me looking in this shot. You ask about cropping in your comments and given my thoughts above I''d have tried a "widescreen" crop that took the bottom off (maybe cut through the bicycle sign and off the top below that bright streetlight - maybe not so much off the bottom?) - this would have reduced the interest in the buildings and made us concentrate on the light trails some more.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> this is ok but there is nothing to differentiate with the other light trail shots. The buildings in the background hold a lot of interest for me and I find this detracts from the light trails.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> it''s an ok shot but nothing "wow"<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that this is a busy scene. The buildings hold interest and then we have the light trails too. Technically this is good. Exposure of the lights is good. Given the light trails are what you were concentrating on the composition is ok - I find that the bright area at the left end of the light trails is where I start looking and then flow along to the right - this seems backwards to how you''d want me looking in this shot. You ask about cropping in your comments and given my thoughts above I''d have tried a "widescreen" crop that took the bottom off (maybe cut through the bicycle sign and off the top below that bright streetlight - maybe not so much off the bottom?) - this would have reduced the interest in the buildings and made us concentrate on the light trails some more. Artistically this is ok but there is nothing to differentiate with the other light trail shots. The buildings in the background hold a lot of interest for me and I find this detracts from the light trails. In summary it''s an ok shot but nothing "wow" Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-02-04 20:28:18.000000', NULL, 0),
