(5858533, 849932, 105457, '<td valign="top">Hi Joshua, greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Regarding your photo:<br/> <br/>Composition<br/>First of all, good usage of a fisheye lens. It''s difficult to take advantage of the distortion factor of such a lens, but in this case you made it revolve around the post, where the Main Str. sign was. You got it all to fit in the photo, with a lot of breathing space.<br/>The man at the right was not totally in the photo, and this just makes it a bit awkward.<br/> <br/>Technique / Processing<br/>Very nicely done on the reflections on the windows, it adds a new point of focus to the shot.<br/>Good exposure, the toning is great.<br/> <br/>Overall<br/>A photo that has probably too much going on, since you''ve got a lot of details that in the end don''t add to the purpose of the challenge.<br/>Although it''s a Main Street challenge, people were expecting to see the actual street.<br/>Still, a 5.64 score and 26th place is not a bad place to be :)<br/> <br/>If you have any questions feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=105457" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">contact me</a>.<br/>Regards,<br/>Joao</td>', 'Hi Joshua, greetings from the Critique Club! Regarding your photo: CompositionFirst of all, good usage of a fisheye lens. It''s difficult to take advantage of the distortion factor of such a lens, but in this case you made it revolve around the post, where the Main Str. sign was. You got it all to fit in the photo, with a lot of breathing space.The man at the right was not totally in the photo, and this just makes it a bit awkward. Technique / ProcessingVery nicely done on the reflections on the windows, it adds a new point of focus to the shot.Good exposure, the toning is great. OverallA photo that has probably too much going on, since you''ve got a lot of details that in the end don''t add to the purpose of the challenge.Although it''s a Main Street challenge, people were expecting to see the actual street.Still, a 5.64 score and 26th place is not a bad place to be :) If you have any questions feel free to contact me.Regards,Joao', '2010-02-08 06:52:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5859385, 849060, 56880, '<td valign="top">This strikes me more as a (very good) "street" photo than a main street one.  The stories here are local and personal: the guy on the phone hearing Vanilla Ice is back on tour, the wall of suits protecting their feeding grounds from encroaching commuters.</td>', 'This strikes me more as a (very good) "street" photo than a main street one.  The stories here are local and personal: the guy on the phone hearing Vanilla Ice is back on tour, the wall of suits protecting their feeding grounds from encroaching commuters.', '2010-02-08 16:43:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5862091, 849909, 56880, '<td valign="top">This reminds me of visiting the small town where my Grandpa lives when I was very young.  All trucks and bricks and weathered buildings, and "one way" for both roads and culture.  Nostalgic.  Great capture.</td>', 'This reminds me of visiting the small town where my Grandpa lives when I was very young.  All trucks and bricks and weathered buildings, and "one way" for both roads and culture.  Nostalgic.  Great capture.', '2010-02-10 15:19:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5870664, 850056, 92577, '<td valign="top">Just got back from holiday and one of the first things I wanted to check out on DPC was how this shot had gone on. Wow! An 8! That makes you a member of a pretty elite club. It also puts you in the number one spot on the D90 home page. Nice to hear you praising the DPC community (I remember you having a little whinge about them sometime last year). It seems the move to Italia has re-stoked the old photographic furnace. So, congrats and bona fortuna.</td>', 'Just got back from holiday and one of the first things I wanted to check out on DPC was how this shot had gone on. Wow! An 8! That makes you a member of a pretty elite club. It also puts you in the number one spot on the D90 home page. Nice to hear you praising the DPC community (I remember you having a little whinge about them sometime last year). It seems the move to Italia has re-stoked the old photographic furnace. So, congrats and bona fortuna.', '2010-02-17 04:59:10.000000', NULL, 0),
